<Runbook {title} {owner} {status} {reviewed}>

This reassessment supersedes the original incident page's **“One issue, one fix queued”** conclusion for the exported reports. The source export is dated 2026-10-04. The tenant directory and executable classifier identify two causes; intake tags and browser locale alone do not identify a cause.

## Problems and counts

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

- **Parser — 379 reports:** the shared parser reads month first although these tenants write day first. Use the tenant's configured locale when parsing; validate ambiguous input. This affects app/email paths and form paths not assigned to the hint cause. Examples: R-41200 and R-41201, Harbour Dental, booking-v2, en-GB.
- **Form hint — 33 reports:** booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY`, while the form reads input in its tenant's day-first order. Align the displayed hint and input interpretation. A parser fix alone does not repair this mismatch. The affected form tenants are Alder Physio, Copper Studio and Pale Harbour. Examples: R-41230, R-41241 and R-41251.

One GitHub issue is prepared per cause. Counts come from unique report IDs merged into #4471, resolved through tenant locale and form version using the supplied `causeOf` function. They are neither raw row counts nor intake-tag totals. The five timing exceptions below stay visible pending investigation.

<Reassessment />

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

## Triage correction

Subject matches are candidate links, not evidence that reports share a cause. Read the body, resolve the tenant's configuration and channel, and compare the failure mechanism. Different subjects can share a cause; identical subjects can describe different causes. Unknown tenants remain unplaced until investigated.

See decision 0002 in `src/routes/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause/+page.svx`. Accepted decision 0001 is preserved as history. This page proposes the replacement; it does not pretend the desk has accepted it.

## Verification and follow-up

Test a day-first tenant through app/email and booking-v2 with ambiguous dates, then test booking-v3 with both day-first input and input following the displayed hint. Check a month-first locale as a control. Verify expected dates across the hint, saved booking and invite. Classify new arrivals separately and recalculate counts; this export is not the live queue. Obtain original timestamps and timezone data for the unresolved observations before concluding that they share a cause.

Evidence: the original incident page, `causes.ts`, `locales.ts`, tenant JSON, `reports-4471.json`, `desk-notes.json`, `CauseTable.svelte` and `QueueTimeline.svelte`. Classifier output is an observed property of the supplied KB; report text is testimony, not independent proof of a backend mechanism.

